+### Time Format Compound
+
+```js
+ms(5400000, { compound: true })       // "1h30m"
+ms(91800000, { compound: true })      // "25h30m"
+ms(-90061000, { compound: true })     // "-25h1m1s"
+```
+
+Output is compatible with Go's `time.ParseDuration`: no spaces, and hours are the largest unit (never days). Zero parts are skipped, leftover milliseconds are dropped, and values under one second give `"0s"`. Takes precedence over `long`.
